@startuml
title Git Branching Structure: main, dev, test, and feature

skinparam state {
  BorderColor #4178BE
  BackgroundColor #EAF4FF
  RoundCorner 10
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF8DC
  BorderColor #E0C14E
}

' ===== BRANCHES =====
state "main branch" as MAIN {
  state "M1\nInitial commit" as M1
  state "M2\nStable release" as M2
  state "M3\nProduction hotfix" as M3
}

state "dev branch" as DEV {
  state "D1\nSync from main" as D1
  state "D2\nIntegration changes" as D2
  state "D3\nPre-release" as D3
}

state "test branch" as TEST {
  state "T1\nPulled from dev" as T1
  state "T2\nTesting & QA" as T2
  state "T3\nApproved for release" as T3
}

state "feature branch" as FEAT {
  state "F1\nStart feature" as F1
  state "F2\nFeature implementation" as F2
  state "F3\nFeature complete" as F3
}

' ===== FLOW =====

' main flow
M1 --> M2
M2 --> M3

' dev branch from main
M1 --> D1
D1 --> D2
D2 --> D3

' feature branch from dev
D1 -down-> F1
F1 --> F2
F2 --> F3
F3 -up-> D2

' dev to test
D3 --> T1 
T1 --> T2
T2 --> T3
T3 --> M3 

' ===== NOTES =====
note top of FEAT
Feature branches are short-lived  
and merged into dev after completion
end note

note top of DEV
dev integrates multiple features  
and is merged into test for QA
end note

note bottom of TEST
test branch ensures stability  
before merging into main
end note

note top of MAIN
main contains production-ready code  
and receives merges only from test
end note

@enduml
